course: dictionary
lesson: 14560
title: Photoshop and fake pictures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Photoshop is a computer program that people use to edit pictures. As a verb, to photoshop means to change a photo on a computer, often to make it look better. Sometimes it means changing a photo to fake something that never happened.
explain: «The model in the magazine had perfect skin, but the picture was badly photoshopped.» Badly photoshopped means the editing was done poorly, so the picture looks fake. The clues «perfect» and «badly» help you see what is going on.
explain: Many pictures in adverts and online have been photoshopped. Bodies, faces and events may look nothing like real life. Before you believe a picture, ask yourself: could this have been changed?
fact: Photoshop is a computer program used to edit pictures. Its name is also a trademark.
fact: To photoshop a photo means to change it on a computer, often to make it look better.
fact: «Photoshop out» means to remove something from a picture, such as a sign or a person.
fact: Fake photoshopped images can spread lies online.
fact: Editing photos is a real skill, and artists and designers use it in their work.
exercise: «The advert showed a perfect beach, but the sea had been photoshopped in.» What does photoshopped mean here? | *Changed on a computer to look different | Printed on paper | Washed clean by the waves | Taken with a very old camera
exercise: Which word means a computer program used to edit pictures? | Scrapbook | Calculator | *Photoshop | Keyboard
exercise: Mia says, «This photo of a flood looks fake.» What might have happened to the photo? | It was printed in colour | It was taken on a sunny day at the beach | *It was photoshopped to fake something that did not happen
test: «Dad said the picture of the giant fish was badly photoshopped.» What does this tell you? | The fish was caught in the sea and weighed | The fish was very heavy | The picture was taken in a museum | *The picture was edited on a computer and may look fake
test: Which is a good question to ask before you believe a picture online? | *Could this picture have been changed? | What is the picture's size in centimetres? | Is the picture in colour or black and white?
exam: Which sentence uses photoshop as a verb, meaning to edit a photo? | *They photoshopped the sky to make it bluer | The Photoshop program is open on my laptop | The photo was printed on glossy paper
